content:
The live Gemini adapter is failing with LanguageError. Please update it to the current Gemini 3.8 Flash Generate Content structured-output format.

Keep the existing LanguageAdapter boundary and deterministic core unchanged.

Use:
- gemini-3.8-flash as the default model;
- stateless generateContent;
- store=false;
- current responseFormat.text.mimeType/schema instead of the legacy responseMimeType/responseJsonSchema fields;
- the existing Pydantic Proposal validation.

Also improve safe diagnostics so provider failures can be distinguished (HTTP/auth/quota/model, timeout, safety stop, invalid JSON/schema) without logging secrets, prompts, user messages, or raw provider bodies.

Update tests/docs as needed and run the full validation suite.

Do not modify quote-service or add another production LLM provider.

The live Gemini integration is working, but Google returned occasional 503 and 429 errors during evaluation.

Finalize the integration:
- keep gemini-3.8-flash as the default model;
- set the LLM deadline to 30 seconds;
- classify transient 5xx responses as language_unavailable;
- keep quota/auth/model errors distinct;
- update the live evaluator so a single provider failure does not abort all 25 cases, and report provider failures separately from extraction-quality failures;
- keep the no-retry policy for Gemini;
- update tests/docs/config examples accordingly.

Do not modify quote-service or the deterministic core.
